course: dictionary
lesson: 8155
title: Rescuer: the one who saves
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A rescuer is a person or animal who saves someone or something from danger. The word comes from rescue, which means to save. The ending -er often means a person who does something: a teacher teaches, a painter paints, so a rescuer rescues.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentences. «Only a trained rescuer goes into the water.» The danger is the water, and the rescuer is the one who goes in safely because they have had training.
explain: Use the swap check. «Heat and too little water can make hikers very ill quickly, and every year rescuers are called to people who ran out of water.» Put in "people who save others from danger" and the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Rescuers can be people or animals, and they are often the heroes in stories. Firefighters, lifeguards, mountain rescue teams and coastguards are all rescuers.
fact: A rescuer is a person or animal who saves someone or something from danger.
fact: Rescuer comes from the word rescue, which means to save.
fact: Firefighters, lifeguards, mountain rescue teams and coastguards are all rescuers.
fact: «Rescuers wash them with washing-up liquid» means that birds covered in spilled oil are cleaned so they can keep warm and fly again.
fact: In first aid, a rescuer must first check that it is safe for themselves before helping anyone else.
exercise: «Only a trained rescuer goes into the water.» Who is allowed into the water? | Anyone who likes swimming | *A trained rescuer | Spilled oil on the sea | A lost girl on the moor
exercise: A rescuer is a person or animal who does what? | Plays music in a band | Writes stories about the past | Sells food in a shop | *Saves someone or something from danger
exercise: Which of these is a rescuer? | A postman delivering letters | *A lifeguard watching the pool | A teacher marking books | A baker making bread
test: Which of these is NOT a rescuer? | *A dentist who checks people's teeth | A firefighter | A coastguard | A mountain rescue team
test: «The first rescuer at the scene knelt beside the boy.» What does rescuer mean here? | A person who shouts at everyone | *A person who saves someone from danger | A person who loses things | A person who takes photos of the crowd
exam: A girl blew her whistle on a moor, and «rescuers heard it and found her quickly.» Which choice best describes the rescuers? | Birds that flew over the moor | A group of walkers looking for a picnic spot | Shops that sold whistles | *Helpers who came to save the lost girl from danger
